Round 5 (review round 3). Base commit 46285c324. 113 mutants on the final code: every earlier one repeated on the new
statement (M, K, C, T, Q, E, V, A, N, R, F, O, B, S, P) plus the new guards: W = charge-only-when-it-fits and the refund's window,
C9 = cost-aware memory, X = after-commit forfeit, Y = provider failures, I/D/G/S4-S5 = send-route order, U = the shared table,
O4 = a refundable route under als.exit, P2/P3 = census (a shared key at another limit; a limiter passed as a value).
Each is run against six integration files (51 tests) and sixteen unit files (196 tests); restored with git checkout after each.
The log opens and closes with a BASELINE run; both are green. 113 of 113 RED, no survivor, no failed apply.

